# Line endings for the launchers, whatever core.autocrlf is on the machine that
# checks this out (Windows checkouts often have it set to true).
#
# cmd.exe misreads labels and `goto` in a batch file with LF line endings, and
# bash reads a CR at the end of a line as part of the command. So each launcher
# keeps the endings its own shell needs, in a clone and in GitHub's
# "Download ZIP" alike.
*.bat      text eol=crlf
*.cmd      text eol=crlf
*.command  text eol=lf
*.sh       text eol=lf
